.B TTL \- TTL set on object
A TTL record is emitted whenever the ttl, grace or keep values for an object is set as well as whether the object is  cacheable or not.
.sp
The format is:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
%s %d %d %d %d [ %d %d %u %u ] %s
|  |  |  |  |    |  |  |  |    |
|  |  |  |  |    |  |  |  |    +\- \(dqcacheable\(dq or \(dquncacheable\(dq
|  |  |  |  |    |  |  |  +\-\-\-\-\-\- Max\-Age from Cache\-Control header
|  |  |  |  |    |  |  +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- Expires header
|  |  |  |  |    |  +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- Date header
|  |  |  |  |    +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- Age (incl Age: header value)
|  |  |  |  +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- Reference time for TTL
|  |  |  +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- Keep
|  |  +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- Grace
|  +\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- TTL
+\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\- \(dqRFC\(dq, \(dqVCL\(dq or \(dqHFP\(dq
